{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "title": "Fenwick plant taxonomy",
  "description": "Taxonomic hierarchy for organizing plant research records and infocards. Botanical ranks are separated from horticultural cultivar/growth-habit groupings.",
  "rank_order": [
    "kingdom",
    "clade",
    "major_clade",
    "order",
    "family",
    "genus",
    "species",
    "cultivar_or_horticultural_group"
  ],
  "rules": [
    "Taxonomic hierarchy is Kingdom → Angiosperms → major clade → order → family → genus → species.",
    "Major clades Eudicots and Monocots are informal clades, not formal Linnaean ranks.",
    "Cultivar groups, growth-habit groups and common horticultural selections are subordinate organizational labels, not botanical ranks.",
    "Use accepted botanical names and record synonyms separately; hybrid notation (×) is retained where applicable.",
    "An infocard is a visual/horticultural representation linked to a taxon; multiple infocards may share the same species taxon.",
    "Do not collapse distinct genera or species because their common names or uses are similar.",
    "Every placement is provisional until exact accepted-name and synonymy review against POWO/WFO; missing taxon-specific authority remains visible.",
    "Coverage spans nonvascular bryophytes, vascular spore plants (lycophytes, ferns and horsetails), gymnosperms, and angiosperms; do not place all plants under flowering plants."
  ],
